];
---
<Guide
  lang="en"
  route="aiDealers"
  title="AI Dealer Blackjack: What It Is, Is It Fair, What Changes"
  h1="AI dealers in blackjack: what they are and what changes for you"
  description="Live casinos are starting to use AI-rendered digital dealers. What they are, who is launching them in 2026, whether the game is fair and why your strategy doesn’t change but card counting dies."
  updated="2026-10-30"
  readMinutes={6}
  faq={faq}
  related={['live', 'sideBets', 'counting', 'strategy']}
>
  <div slot="top">
    <div class="tldr"><p><strong>Quick answer:</strong> an AI dealer is a computer-generated dealer that replaces the person filmed in a live studio. In 2026 several studios are launching them, starting with blackjack. For you as a player: <strong>basic strategy doesn’t change</strong> (it depends on the rules, not on the dealer), fairness depends on <strong>how the cards are generated and whether the operator is licensed</strong>, and if each hand is shuffled fresh, <strong>card counting is impossible</strong>.</p></div>
  </div>

  <h2 id="what">What an AI dealer is</h2>
  <p>Classic live blackjack films a real dealer with real cards in a studio. The new “AI dealers” replace that person with a digital one. The most talked-about approach records real dealers with motion capture and turns them into animated <strong>digital clones</strong>, rendered in real time with a video game engine and streamed to your screen. The dealer looks human, talks and reacts, but no one is standing at a table.</p>
  <p>For the casino the appeal is cost: no studios open around the clock, no shifts, no need for dealers in every language.</p>

  <h2 id="who">Who is launching them</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Avanti Studios</strong>, founded by a co-founder of LeoVegas, builds games with AI-rendered digital dealers. It chose <strong>Spain</strong> as its first regulated market, with live blackjack among its first games, and signed a distribution deal with Entain.</li>
    <li><strong>Playgon</strong>, a Canadian supplier, announced its own AI dealers, rolling out baccarat first, then blackjack, then roulette.</li>
    <li><strong>Evolution</strong>, the biggest live casino supplier, has said publicly that it expects human dealers to keep dominating.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>So, as of late 2026, these games exist but are still new: you will find them in some regulated markets, alongside traditional live tables.</p>

  <h2 id="fair">Is it fair?</h2>
  <p>The key question isn’t who deals but <strong>where the cards come from</strong>:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Physical shoe, filmed:</strong> classic live blackjack. You see real cards.</li>
    <li><strong>Random number generator (RNG):</strong> the cards are picked by software, as in any online blackjack. An animated dealer on top of an RNG is, mathematically, a regular online game with a nicer presentation.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>An RNG game is fair when the operator is licensed and the generator is audited by an independent lab. In Spain that means a DGOJ licence; other countries have their own regulator. Avoid unlicensed sites, with or without AI.</p>

  <h2 id="strategy">Does strategy change?</h2>
  <p>No. The correct play depends on the <strong>rules</strong>, not on the dealer’s face. Before you play, open the table’s rules panel and check: number of decks, whether the dealer checks for blackjack (hole card) or not, whether they hit soft 17, doubling and splitting rules, surrender, and that blackjack pays 3:2. Then use the matching chart in our <a href={routes.strategy.en}>interactive strategy chart</a>.</p>
  <p>Most live and digital tables use European rules with no hole card: against a 10, you don’t double 11 or split 8-8. We explain why in <a href={routes.live.en}>live blackjack</a>.</p>

  <h2 id="counting">The end of card counting online</h2>
  <p>Counting works only when the cards dealt affect the ones that remain. With an RNG that reshuffles every hand, that link disappears: the chance of the next card is always the same, and counting gives you exactly nothing. Even classic live tables reshuffle early enough to make counting almost useless. If you want to understand counting, read <a href={routes.counting.en}>how to count cards</a>, but don’t expect it to work on a screen.</p>

  <h2 id="side-bets">Same side bets, same cost</h2>
  <p>Digital tables push side bets just as hard as live ones. 21+3 and Perfect Pairs carry a house edge several times higher than the main hand: we calculated it in <a href={routes.sideBets.en}>blackjack side bets</a>.</p>

  <h2 id="honest">An honest reminder</h2>
  <p>A dealer who never gets tired and a table that’s always open make it easier to play longer than you meant to. Set a limit before you start, and if it stops being fun, see <a href={routes.responsible.en}>responsible gambling</a>. To learn strategy without money, use the <a href={routes.simulator.en}>free practice table</a>.</p>
</Guide>
